  "schema:name": "KGDmnOutputClause",
  "dcterms:title": "Knowledge graph L2-DMN: DMN Output Clause",
  "dcterms:description": "An output column. The BCG table's four are Care Plan, Guidance displayed to health worker, Annotations and Reference(s). These are column DEFINITIONS in a decision table, not clinical records: no edge from this class reaches an execution artefact, and none may. serialisedAs is outputEntry or annotationEntry -- DMN splits the columns across two element types and the split is positional, so recording it is what lets a rule's cells be matched back to their columns. isReferenceColumn marks the L1 column, found by its description rather than its index. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/dmn-output-clause.",
